2. Deep Dive: Component Breakdown
A. Plant Level (Inside the Factory Network)
Each plant PC runs local SCADA/iNDUS services and a PostgreSQL database.

What we add:

Indus.RemoteMonitoring.Api: A lightweight, read-only adapter service listening only on loopback (127.0.0.1:7000). It queries the local PostgreSQL DB for trends/events and reads live tags from the local cache.

cloudflared Service: An outbound tunnel connector.

Why:

Air-gapping SCADA: The API only allows Read operations. It is physically impossible to issue a breaker trip or setpoint change from the mobile app because those write routes do not exist.

Loopback Binding: Listening on 127.0.0.1 ensures that even local network devices cannot hit this API directly without local authorization.

       [ Local Plant PC ]
       ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ PostgreSQL DB  ──(Read-Only SQL)──┐                    │
       │                                   ▼                    │
       │ Local SCADA Service ─(Live Cache)─► Site Monitoring API│
       │                                         ▲              │
       │                                         │ (localhost)  │
       │                                   [cloudflared] ───────┼───► (Outbound Encrypted Tunnel)
       └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
B. Security & Transport (Cloudflare Tunnel + Zero Trust)
What we are doing:
We establish outbound TLS tunnels on port 7844 from each plant PC to Cloudflare's edge, assigning each site a unique URL (e.g., site101-api.indusautomation.com). We protect this URL using Cloudflare Access Service Auth.

Why:

No Inbound Open Ports: Standard remote access requires forwarding ports (like 5432 or 80/443) on the plant router, exposing the network to port scanners and brute-force attacks. Cloudflare Tunnels initiate outbound connections only—the plant router blocks all incoming connections.

Service Tokens: Mobile phones never communicate directly with the site tunnel URL. Only the central AWS Gateway holds the CF-Access-Client-Id and CF-Access-Client-Secret to bypass the Zero Trust firewall.

