6. Key Takeaways & Rules to Remember
SCADA Isolation: Remote write capability is intentionally omitted from Release 1 to prevent unauthorized control actions.

Database Integrity: DynamoDB handles central application metadata (users/permissions). Raw plant tag history stays in local PostgreSQL databases at each site.

Fail-Closed Security: If the metadata database is unreachable or a user's token expires, the gateway defaults to blocking all requests. Local plant operations remain unaffected if internet connectivity drops.
